# Line endings here are correctness, not style. A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for
# an interpreter named `bash\r`, so a hook exits 127 instead of 2 -- and a PreToolUse hook
# that does not exit 2 does not block. Commit this file: untracked, it governs only the
# working tree it sits in, and a clone on a machine with core.autocrlf=true undoes it.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*       text=auto
